"Stephen Lattanzi" <lattanzi@myeastern.com> wrote:

>My kids love to play NetHack on my PC running Windows XP, but I don't want 
>them to use the account with Administrator privileges.  Is there any way for 
>me to set up NetHack (either tty or graphical interface) for use on a 
>non-Administrator account?

NetHack does not need admin rights on Windows. Maybe you have
accidentally installed it into a directory where only you have writing
rights, and not a group to which your kids belong. To easily check and
change the rights, use "cacls" on the command line. ("cacls /?" prints a
help text.)
